Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?hyundai:=20FCA11=20CAL=20scripted=20level=20rea?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ches=20the=20wire=20=E2=80=94=20planner=20term=20from=20the=20r?=
 =?UTF-8?q?aw=20ask=20under=20cal?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The cal path computes the planner term as
dec_cmd_from_accel(min(accel, FCA11_BRAKE_ONSET_ACCEL)), so a COASTING planner contributed
dec_cmd_from_accel(-0.5) = 8 LSB. The scripted level then entered as max(planner_term,
cal_level), which made every scripted level <= 8 degenerate to 8 on the wire: the 4-8 LSB
measurement ladder could not command its own levels.

Under cal (cal_on), compute the planner term from the RAW ask. When the planner is BRAKING
(accel <= ONSET_ACCEL) it is a no-op for the onset clamp, so the mapping there is unchanged
and max() still means "cal only ADDS braking". It does NOT mean that inside the release band
(-0.5 < accel <= -0.3): there dec_cmd_from_accel(-0.49) = 0, the scripted level is
authoritative, and the cal frame may carry LESS than the 0049 release-band floor (8 LSB) --
it can undercut production there. That is bounded (the planner asked <= 0.5 m/s^2, gas is
forced to 0 on a cal frame, arming needs 5 s in band + lead >= 60 m + an owner tap) and it
applies to cal frames only. The affine sub-branch takes the same raw ask; it is wire-neutral
at levels >= CAL_MIN_LSB (the affine onset term is 1 LSB) and keeps both branches consistent.

Gated on cal_on: with cal off `_ask_for_law` IS `accel_ask`, so the planner path is unchanged
(proven byte-identical to the parent build over all three recorded shadow streams, with
personalities forced to 0/1/2 in three cal-off configurations).

Panda-side authority is untouched: same frame shape (Warn 3, CmdAct 1, DecCmdAct 0, Prefill 1),
same +RATE_STEP ramp over the last SENT frame, same 30 LSB gate, one passive close.

Adds tests/test_fca11_cal_level.py (10 tests): the coasting-planner ladder 4/5/6/7/8 must
deliver the exact scripted level (fails on the parent tree for 4-7), a release-band ask
(-0.49 and -0.4) carries the scripted level rather than the clamp floor, a soft ask is not a
hidden 8, a braking planner still wins over the scripted level, the contract is preserved, and
the cal-off planner path is pinned.
---
 opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py  |  11 +-
 .../car/hyundai/tests/test_fca11_cal_level.py | 232 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 241 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/tests/test_fca11_cal_level.py

diff --git a/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py b/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py
index b9ca367..71c878f 100644
--- a/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py
+++ b/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/fca11_long.py
@@ -1706,10 +1706,17 @@ class Fca11LongBrake:
         # the ESC never sees a 0 mid-episode (a 0 would be an immediate release, defeating the hysteresis).
         # 0041: the OPT-IN affine law (self.affine_gain, DEFAULT OFF) replaces the through-origin inverse with the
         # fitted affine plant inverse (dec_cmd_from_accel_affine); OFF -> byte-identical to 0040.
+        # 0050 CAL: under cal the planner term is computed from the RAW ask, NOT the onset-clamped one. The scripted
+        # level below enters as a FLOOR (`max()`), so a COASTING planner must contribute 0 -- but the -0.5 onset clamp
+        # maps through the 0.67 inverse to 8, so every scripted level <= 8 became 8 on the wire (the degenerate class;
+        # wsSTOP/m57 MEASUREMENT-5-7.md §0.3). A planner that IS braking (accel <= ONSET_ACCEL) is a no-op for the
+        # clamp, so there the mapping is unchanged and `max()` still means "cal only ADDS braking". Gated on cal_on:
+        # with cal off `_ask_for_law` IS `accel_ask`, so the planner path is byte-identical (identity.py).
+        _ask_for_law = accel if cal_on else accel_ask
         if self.affine_gain:
-          dec_cmd = dec_cmd_from_accel_affine(accel_ask)
+          dec_cmd = dec_cmd_from_accel_affine(_ask_for_law)
         else:
-          dec_cmd = dec_cmd_from_accel(accel_ask)
+          dec_cmd = dec_cmd_from_accel(_ask_for_law)
         # production tiering of the planner ask (unchanged when cal is off -> byte-identical). 0041: under the affine
         # law the command may legitimately taper to 0 (no honest request), so the floor is the honest level, not the
         # fixed 1 the through-origin law uses; OFF keeps the 0040 clamp exactly (raw CR_VSM_DecCmd >= 1).
diff --git a/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/tests/test_fca11_cal_level.py b/opendbc/sunnypilot/car/hyundai/tests/test_fca11_cal_level.py
